    {"id": 1, "narration": "Today we learn Python lists. A list stores many values in one variable. Let's build one step by step.",
     "remotion": {"type": "TitleCard", "props": {"title": "Python Lists", "subtitle": "One variable, many values", "badge": "DAY 1 • PYTHON LISTS", "tags": ["Python", "Lists", "Beginner"]}}},

    {"id": 2, "narration": "First, we create a list called fruits with three items. Next, append adds kiwi at the end. Index zero gives the first item, apple. And len tells us how many items there are.",
     "remotion": {"type": "TypingCode", "type_anchor": "First,",
       "props": {"filename": "lists.py", "language": "python", "code": "fruits = [\"apple\", \"mango\", \"banana\"]\nfruits.append(\"kiwi\")\nprint(fruits[0])\nprint(len(fruits))", "highlightLines": [2]},
       "popups": [
         {"anchor": "append", "text": "append() adds at the END", "kind": "tip", "x": "72%", "y": "30%"},
         {"anchor": "Index", "text": "Index starts at 0", "kind": "tip", "x": "72%", "y": "62%"},
         {"anchor": "len", "text": "len() counts items", "kind": "note", "x": "72%", "y": "80%"}
       ]}},

    {"id": 3, "narration": "Run the file, and you see the output. Apple first, then four, because we added kiwi.",
     "remotion": {"type": "TerminalRun", "props": {"command": "python lists.py", "output": ["apple", "4"]}}},

    {"id": 4, "narration": "A tuple is fixed after creation. A list can change. That is the big difference between them.",
     "remotion": {"type": "ComparisonCard", "props": {"title": "List vs Tuple",
        "leftTitle": "Tuple", "leftPoints": ["Fixed after creation", "Uses parentheses ()", "Cannot append"],
        "rightTitle": "List", "rightPoints": ["Add and remove items", "Uses square brackets []", "Most used in Python"]},
       "popups": [{"anchor": "change", "text": "Lists can change", "kind": "note", "x": "50%", "y": "14%"}]}},

    {"id": 5, "narration": "Recap. Lists store many values. Append adds at the end. Index starts at zero. Tuples are fixed. Practice by making your own list today.",
